I can not recommend Xenophon&#x27;s Anabasis (AKA March Of The Ten Thousand) enough.<p>I&#x27;m rereading it for the fourth time, in less than 2 years. There&#x27;s a variety of themes:<p>- political intrigue;
- religion;
- moral, ethics;
- companionship;
- brotherhood;<p>etc. Xenophon is eloquent and straight to the point, I really like his approach in this narration.<p>Now, on the topic of &quot;rereading&quot;, I&#x27;ve often thought that maybe I should (have) read other books; that perhaps I was &quot;spending too much time&quot; in one book, but I just don&#x27;t care enough to ruminate on this thought, and besides, there&#x27;s always something new to learn from it.<p>Concurrently I&#x27;m reading &quot;Crime &amp; Punishment&quot;, which I also recommend.
